202
00:18:46.336 --> 00:18:51.836
Speaker 4: Hey, pay attention. So one day, their
troubles compounded.

203
00:18:52.776 --> 00:18:58.216
Speaker 4: A monster attacked the village,
carrying the weak and the sickly back to its
cave to

204
00:18:58.256 --> 00:18:59.116
Speaker 4: devour them.

205
00:19:00.156 --> 00:19:01.236
Speaker 5: What did they do about it?

206
00:19:02.356 --> 00:19:07.656
Speaker 4: Well, they surrounded the mouth of
the cave with explosives and waited for the
beast

207
00:19:07.696 --> 00:19:13.696
Speaker 4: to exit. And when it finally did,
they detonated the trap. The monster was

208
00:19:13.776 --> 00:19:18.856
Speaker 4: ripped to shreds by the explosion.
Bloody chunks rained down everywhere.

209
00:19:20.296 --> 00:19:23.036
Speaker 5: Whoa. So they lived happily ever
after?

210
00:19:24.516 --> 00:19:30.416
Speaker 4: Hell no. They lived in abject
poverty. Life was short, brutal, and filled

211
00:19:30.456 --> 00:19:32.076
Speaker 4: with unnecessary suffering.

212
00:19:34.796 --> 00:19:35.796
Speaker 4: So are you tired now?

213
00:19:36.216 --> 00:19:42.036
Speaker 1: Fleabag's tan face was covered in
shadow. Ethan switched to infrared. He did not

214
00:19:42.096 --> 00:19:45.356
Speaker 1: look tired. Perhaps another story
then.

215
00:19:46.116 --> 00:19:47.416
Speaker 5: Are you really a preacher?

216
00:19:48.696 --> 00:19:52.376
Speaker 4: I used to be. Now I preach a
different gospel.

217
00:19:53.276 --> 00:19:53.636
Speaker 5: What?

218
00:19:54.556 --> 00:19:55.996
Speaker 4: The gospel of lead.

219
00:19:58.616 --> 00:20:00.596
Speaker 5: Why do you say things like that?

220
00:20:01.296 --> 00:20:06.116
Speaker 4: I don't know. It just kinda comes
out. Think I might be sick.

221
00:20:07.276 --> 00:20:08.116
Speaker 5: In your brain?

222
00:20:08.116 --> 00:20:10.676
Speaker 4: [laughs] I guess so.

223
00:20:12.776 --> 00:20:13.516
Speaker 5: It's okay.

224
00:20:14.636 --> 00:20:19.856
Speaker 1: Then the kid leaned against Ethan and
closed his eyes. And even though he didn't

225
00:20:19.896 --> 00:20:23.396
Speaker 1: need to sleep, Ethan closed his eyes
too.

226
00:20:24.916 --> 00:20:28.196
Speaker 5: Can you protect us from the real
monsters?

227
00:20:29.056 --> 00:20:31.255
Speaker 4: I'm going to try.

228
00:20:33.176 --> 00:20:38.996
Speaker 1: Fleabag let out a long breath, and a
minute later he was snoring, his

229
00:20:39.116 --> 00:20:45.016
Speaker 1: small head resting on Ethan's armless
torso. If he didn't get repairs soon,

230
00:20:45.116 --> 00:20:51.076
Speaker 1: though, he wouldn't be protecting
anyone. It was unlikely he'd be

231
00:20:51.156 --> 00:20:56.936
Speaker 1: able to kill a second demon with his
teeth. Then this

232
00:20:57.036 --> 00:21:02.596
Speaker 1: tiny person would die. A knife of
pain made it through his pain

233
00:21:02.656 --> 00:21:07.776
Speaker 1: filters. This was not a physical
pain. It was something

234
00:21:08.736 --> 00:21:14.636
Speaker 1: unfamiliar and far more frightening.
What if

235
00:21:15.196 --> 00:21:16.976
Speaker 1: he could not save them?

236
00:21:17.036 --> 00:21:32.016
Speaker 1: [gentle music]

237
00:21:32.096 --> 00:21:36.156
Speaker 1: Sometime before dawn, Ethan stirred
to the sound of a voice.

238
00:21:36.816 --> 00:21:39.436
Speaker 5: Number Four? Number Four, can you
hear me?

239
00:21:40.516 --> 00:21:46.376
Speaker 1: He scanned the room, careful not to
stir the sleeping Fleabag. There was

240
00:21:46.456 --> 00:21:47.916
Speaker 1: no one in the room.

241
00:21:48.816 --> 00:21:49.716
Speaker 5: It's Sister Fran.

242
00:21:50.856 --> 00:21:56.156
Speaker 1: Coming from his mind, then. Great.
That was the last place he needed more

243
00:21:56.336 --> 00:21:56.956
Speaker 1: voices.

244
00:21:57.836 --> 00:22:00.076
Speaker 4: Fran, this is Pastor Cutter.

245
00:22:00.816 --> 00:22:04.396
Speaker 5: You're alive. Ha. I told you it would
work.

246
00:22:05.196 --> 00:22:06.656
Speaker 4: What is this?

247
00:22:07.336 --> 00:22:09.696
Speaker 5: A radio. You have a receiver in your
spine.

248
00:22:10.956 --> 00:22:12.516
Speaker 4: And why?

249
00:22:13.456 --> 00:22:16.656
Speaker 5: So we can monitor you, obviously.

250
00:22:17.696 --> 00:22:18.816
Speaker 1: They'd been watching him?

251
00:22:19.696 --> 00:22:25.036
Speaker 5: Listen, I don't have long. Things
have gone crazy in Last Respite. Gabriel went

252
00:22:25.456 --> 00:22:31.016
Speaker 5: rogue. The advanced clinic is done.
Me and the other nuns got out, though. Oh, and

253
00:22:31.056 --> 00:22:32.056
Speaker 5: you have a bomb in you.

254
00:22:35.536 --> 00:22:36.076
Speaker 5: Number Four?

255
00:22:37.396 --> 00:22:38.056
Speaker 4: I'm here.

256
00:22:38.795 --> 00:22:41.136
Speaker 5: Okay. Whew. I thought she blew you
up.

257
00:22:41.716 --> 00:22:42.436
Speaker 4: Is that a risk?

258
00:22:43.556 --> 00:22:48.296
Speaker 5: Yeah, for sure. That's why I'm
sending you a patch. Erica can probably hear
this,

259
00:22:48.376 --> 00:22:54.076
Speaker 5: though. They know everything you're
doing, even if they can't blow you up, yet. So

260
00:22:54.416 --> 00:22:58.696
Speaker 5: you should probably come up with a
reason why they shouldn't blow you up until the

261
00:22:58.756 --> 00:23:03.216
Speaker 5: patch is done. The patch will totally
disable your receiver, so you're going to have

262
00:23:03.256 --> 00:23:03.816
Speaker 5: to go dark.

263
00:23:03.876 --> 00:23:06.716
Speaker 4: [sighs]

264
00:23:06.796 --> 00:23:12.496
Speaker 1: He hadn't even realized he had a
radio receiver. What else did he not know about?

265
00:23:13.096 --> 00:23:18.536
Speaker 1: Why play games like this? And a bomb.

266
00:23:19.136 --> 00:23:21.696
Speaker 4: Because I haven't completed my
mission.

267
00:23:22.836 --> 00:23:23.616
Speaker 5: Your what?

268
00:23:24.236 --> 00:23:26.436
Speaker 4: I'm going to kill the Stalker.

269
00:23:27.236 --> 00:23:32.756
Speaker 5: Listen, we've treated you more like a
project than a person since you woke up,

270
00:23:33.036 --> 00:23:38.156
Speaker 5: and I wanted to say sorry. You don't
have to do this.

271
00:23:39.176 --> 00:23:44.396
Speaker 1: She wasn't doing a very good job of
not getting him blown up. Another voice entered

272
00:23:44.416 --> 00:23:49.716
Speaker 1: his mind then, because why not? That
made four now, by his count.

273
00:23:50.576 --> 00:23:54.216
Speaker 1: Bishop Erica Long said only one word.

274
00:23:54.876 --> 00:23:55.116
Speaker 5: How?

275
00:23:56.576 --> 00:23:58.516
Speaker 4: I need ammunition and repairs.

276
00:23:59.876 --> 00:24:00.036
Speaker 5: No.

277
00:24:01.916 --> 00:24:06.556
Speaker 5: You have 48 hours, then we're sending
a salvage crew for your parts.

278
00:24:07.676 --> 00:24:10.176
Speaker 1: Erica said nothing else after that.

279
00:24:12.396 --> 00:24:12.776
Speaker 4: Fran?

280
00:24:13.676 --> 00:24:17.676
Speaker 5: I'm here, but not for long. We're
heading for New Hope.

281
00:24:19.156 --> 00:24:21.216
Speaker 4: Is that, uh, wise?

282
00:24:22.076 --> 00:24:27.956
Speaker 5: Probably not, but it's not like we
can survive in the outskirts. It hasn't worked

283
00:24:28.016 --> 00:24:29.756
Speaker 5: out too well for you, has it?

284
00:24:31.266 --> 00:24:36.306
Speaker 2: If you survive, come find us and
we'll patch you up. God go with you, Number
Four. I

285
00:24:36.366 --> 00:24:36.586
Speaker 2: mean,

286
00:24:38.146 --> 00:24:40.906
Speaker 2: Ethan. You want to be called Ethan,
right?

287
00:24:42.046 --> 00:24:42.906
Speaker 4: That is my name.

288
00:24:44.026 --> 00:24:46.606
Speaker 2: Right. Bye, Ethan.

289
00:24:47.766 --> 00:24:53.446
Speaker 1: A moment later, an icon appeared in
his HUD. Secure patch. Update

290
00:24:53.986 --> 00:24:54.986
Speaker 1: Y/in.

291
00:24:56.026 --> 00:24:57.266
Speaker 4: Oh, hell yes.

292
00:24:58.266 --> 00:25:01.966
Speaker 1: Permissions error. Admin approval
required.

293
00:25:02.686 --> 00:25:07.446
Speaker 4: You gotta be kidding me. And who are
the admins?

294
00:25:08.306 --> 00:25:11.586
Speaker 1: Hiro Saitama, Gabriel Klein.

295
00:25:12.186 --> 00:25:13.006
Speaker 4: Wait, that's it?

296
00:25:13.926 --> 00:25:19.826
Speaker 1: There were only two admins, and one
of them was already dead. The other,

297
00:25:20.086 --> 00:25:22.446
Speaker 1: from the sound of it, wasn't far from
it.

298
00:25:22.846 --> 00:25:27.006
Speaker 4: And what happens if I try to remove
the bomb myself?

299
00:25:27.866 --> 00:25:33.286
Speaker 1: Never mind that he didn't have any
arms. The answer came back from his second mind

300
00:25:33.346 --> 00:25:34.266
Speaker 1: immediately.

301
00:25:35.866 --> 00:25:37.086
Speaker 1: Detonation.

302
00:25:39.066 --> 00:25:44.586
Speaker 1: 48 hours to kill something nearly
unkillable, with no arms

303
00:25:45.406 --> 00:25:50.746
Speaker 1: and no weapons. He looked down at
Fleabag, who was stirring awake,

304
00:25:52.126 --> 00:25:57.006
Speaker 1: and nine-year-olds notwithstanding,
no allies.

305
00:25:58.946 --> 00:26:04.806
Speaker 1: Sometimes the Lord giveth, and
sometimes the Lord took you for all you were

306
00:26:04.886 --> 00:26:08.546
Speaker 1: worth. Sure would be nice to have a
little more of the former.

307
00:26:09.366 --> 00:26:12.746
Speaker 4: Say, Fleabag, do you know any
mechanics?

308
00:26:13.886 --> 00:26:19.486
Speaker 1: The boy stood up, walked over to the
side of the room, and began peeing against the

309
00:26:19.566 --> 00:26:19.986
Speaker 1: wall.

310
00:26:21.226 --> 00:26:25.126
Speaker 6: Oh, sure, I know a guy. He makes
weapons for the king.

311
00:26:27.086 --> 00:26:30.206
Speaker 4: And this person, can he be trusted?

312
00:26:31.186 --> 00:26:31.626
Speaker 6: I don't know.

313
00:26:32.826 --> 00:26:38.825
Speaker 1: Ethan sighed and leaned his head back
against the wall. He looked up at the ceiling

314
00:26:38.906 --> 00:26:44.126
Speaker 1: rafters, uncertain whether there was
any divinity in that direction,

315
00:26:44.626 --> 00:26:49.846
Speaker 1: or just termites. Then he muttered a
prayer under his breath.

316
00:26:50.786 --> 00:26:55.926
Speaker 4: God, if you're up there, you know I'm
trying to go to bat for you,

317
00:26:57.646 --> 00:27:02.446
Speaker 4: but I'm gonna need arms to swing it.
A little help would be nice.

318
00:27:04.366 --> 00:27:10.246
Speaker 1: Only silence answered. Well, that was
how most prayers went.

319
00:27:10.926 --> 00:27:14.806
Speaker 1: Ethan guessed there was only one way
to find out if they were gonna get answered.

320
00:27:15.666 --> 00:27:17.846
Speaker 4: All right, take me to this
weaponsmith.

321
00:27:19.086 --> 00:27:22.206
Speaker 1: Fleabag turned around and grinned.

322
00:27:22.786 --> 00:27:26.526
Speaker 4: And wash your hands, boy. Didn't you
learn anything from my story?

323
00:27:26.526 --> 00:28:08.886
Speaker 4: [rock music]

324
00:28:08.946 --> 00:28:12.946
Speaker 1: Bishop Erica Long poked at her black
eye in the mirror.

325
00:28:13.746 --> 00:28:15.026
Speaker 2: Seriously, Gabriel.

326
00:28:15.986 --> 00:28:21.386
Speaker 1: Who had known the old man could throw
a punch like that? He didn't really think she

327
00:28:21.426 --> 00:28:27.406
Speaker 1: was going to detonate the cyborg at
full power, did he? It was variable strength.

328
00:28:28.146 --> 00:28:33.586
Speaker 1: In God's name, there were people in
that church. She wasn't a monster. Except,

329
00:28:34.926 --> 00:28:39.906
Speaker 1: the cyborg hadn't failed. It had won
the day,

330
00:28:40.886 --> 00:28:41.566
Speaker 1: somehow.

331
00:28:43.326 --> 00:28:46.046
Speaker 2: No, you are not the bad guy here.

332
00:28:46.326 --> 00:28:48.066
Speaker 1: There was a knock at the bathroom
door.

333
00:28:48.666 --> 00:28:51.826
Speaker 6: Madam, there are several urgent
matters that need your attention.

334
00:28:52.486 --> 00:28:53.466
Speaker 2: I'll be out in a moment.

335
00:28:54.066 --> 00:28:59.326
Speaker 1: Couldn't she get a moment's rest? Why
did everything fall on her?

336
00:28:59.986 --> 00:29:04.706
Speaker 6: Bishop, we found an undocumented,
unsanctioned weapons system in the advanced

337
00:29:04.766 --> 00:29:05.046
Speaker 6: clinic.

338
00:29:06.346 --> 00:29:10.466
Speaker 2: That's redundant. If it's
unsanctioned, it's obviously undocumented.

339
00:29:13.286 --> 00:29:15.426
Speaker 2: Ugh. Fine. Fine.

340
00:29:16.146 --> 00:29:20.746
Speaker 1: Best to deal with this right away.
Lord knew if she took the time to put on some

341
00:29:20.826 --> 00:29:25.646
Speaker 1: makeup, there would be a hostage
crisis, a strike, and maybe the Lord of Darkness

342
00:29:25.726 --> 00:29:27.306
Speaker 1: itself would pay them a visit.
